+// ASTROHYBRID_RUN_MESH=1 (default 0): a mesh-shader draw without indirect arguments may record a run
+// (and so be continued). Its stage information is a function of the registers and device limits
+// (FinishMeshStage), which the structure key covers, and its per-draw work (index segments, group
+// counts, draw dwords, the index range for the shader's reads) runs on every draw, continuation or
+// not. A mesh draw with indirect arguments ends the rendering instance to convert them, so it never
+// records a run and never continues one (it falls back late). At the Sky Garden ~155 draws a frame
+// are mesh draws, ~93 of them with the previous draw's structure key.
+// Mesh programs read their indices by address, so they bind the fault buffer: with the switch on,
+// a program without address writes that binds it may form runs too (draws of any stage). The
+// shaders only mark missing pages there; the buffer is processed at the next garbage collection,
+// not per draw, and each draw's address ranges are still synchronized (PrepareBda) as on the
+// normal path.
+[[nodiscard]] bool MeshRunsEnabled();
